/**

\page page_version_control_home Version Control (Git)

\tableofcontents

The project is hosted on GitHub. You
find the repository at https://github.com/tobiasweinzierl/peano. We try to give
all interested colleagues access to the repository including some write
permissions, but we do protect some branches. If you want to have write access 
to a certain branch, please contact the team, and we will subsequently assign
you a user name through GitInvite.


## Branch structure

Our main branch is called p4, as we work with Peano 4. This one is protected
and serves as our release branch. The old main branch holds the previous 3rd
generation of Peano. We do not maintain it anymore. This old version also does
not contain any extension build with Peano, i.e. there's no ExaHyPE in there
and no ExaParty.


@dot
digraph branches {
  rankdir=TB;
  nodesep=0.15;
  ranksep=0.4;
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, height=0.3];
  edge [arrowhead=none, color="#888888"];

  p4 [fillcolor="#1f4e79", fontcolor=white];

  node [fillcolor="#9dc3e6"];
  peano; exahype; exagrype; exaparty; mghype;
  p4 -> {peano exahype exagrype exaparty mghype};

  node [fillcolor="#fbe5d6", style="rounded,filled,dashed"];
  peano    -> {"peano-load-balancing" "peano-taskgraph" "peano-logging" "peano-..."};
  exahype  -> {"exahype-checkpointing" "exahype-task-fusion" "exahype-..."};
  exagrype -> {"exagrype-abc" "exagrype-..."};
  exaparty -> {"exaparty-..."};
  mghype   -> {"mghype-..."};
}
@enddot

The release branch p4 (dark) and the top-level branches (blue) are
persistent. The subbranches (orange, dashed) are not: they are created for a
particular feature or fix, merged back into their top-level branch, and then
deleted.
Any active user can create temporary subbranches and ask for a mege, but only
few people are allowed to approve the merge.
Obviously, users can fork out arbitrarily under their own temporary branches.


<br /><br />
<div style="background-color: #fcc ; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid green;">
We appreciate your contributions. To make work easier for the consortium, please  
either work within a organisation such as ExaGRyPE or your own, private fork.
Further to that, please refrain from merging into p4 or to commit PRs against p4.
Pick one of its direct children as fork target. 
</div>


## Naming conventions

If you create a new branch, please follow the two naming approaches:

1. Create a hierarchical representation such as exagrype-taskgraph-bugfix
   which highlights that this branch is a subbranch of taskgraph which in
   turn is a subbranch of particles.
2. Use your username followed by a slash as name prefix if you want to 
   flag that you are working on this piece and noone else should interfer
   for the time being.

The second version puts additional emphasis on who "owns" a certain branch,
while the first one highlights the hierarchical relationships. Multi-user
branches or top-level branches do not have a name prefix.

*/
